{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"callous-wavy-kite","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Found by the evidence pass on ticket sole-curbable-stinkpot (9a71-ba9b-89d0-4cb8), which showed these runs were MISATTRIBUTED to ACLI 'command cancelled'.\n\nTwo failed Reconcile Bridge runs converged the reconcile and then failed only in the opt-in continuous-loop re-dispatch step:\n\n- run 31129551929 (2026-08-06T23:01Z) and run 31129431096 (2026-08-06T22:58Z), both: 'could not create workflow dispatch event: HTTP 422: Cannot trigger a workflow_dispatch on a disabled workflow (.../actions/workflows/302389202/dispatches)'.\n\nThe reconcile work itself SUCCEEDED in both. The run is marked red purely because the self-rescheduling chain could not re-seed while the workflow was disabled. That is arguably not a failure: the */20 schedule is documented as the backstop for exactly this case. Consider treating a 422-disabled-workflow re-dispatch as a benign no-op (warn, exit 0) rather than failing an otherwise-converged pass, since a red run here also trips the heartbeat/alerting for a non-problem.\n\nSee the 'Re-dispatch to sustain the continuous loop (opt-in)' step in .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml.","id":"8aed-e264-7112-4c2f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconcile Bridge continuous-loop re-dispatch fails HTTP 422 on a disabled workflow"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786517403248052001,"uuid":"b50dae84-87a1-421a-a057-5bdffee5318b"}